# Files here are NOT uploaded and NOT served: wrangler drops them from the asset
# manifest entirely.
#
# Context: wrangler.jsonc sets assets.directory ".", so a LOCAL `wrangler deploy`
# from this directory would publish everything present on disk — including
# working output that is deliberately gitignored and has never been reviewed.
#
# The live site does not go out this way: it is deployed by GitHub Actions
# (.github/workflows/deploy-dashboard.yml) via `aws s3 sync` from a fresh
# checkout, which by construction contains only git-tracked files. That path is
# already safe. This file closes the local-deploy path so both agree.
#
# The rule: anything tracked in git is reviewed and publishable; anything
# gitignored is local working output and must not be deployed. Keep this in sync
# with .gitignore's reports/ entries.
#
# Nothing the live site needs is excluded: versions.json is the only file fetched
# at runtime, and realvuln-data.js / assets/ are files, not directories.

/compare/
/vc-*/
/realvuln-*/

# Deploy plumbing, not site content.
/wrangler.jsonc
/.deploy-trigger
